    "title": "Sweden Defeats United States in World Junior Hockey Championship; Quarterfinal Matchups Set",
    "text": "• Sweden defeated the United States 6-3 in the world junior hockey championship on Wednesday night.\n• Lucas Pettersson and Eddie Genborg each scored twice for Sweden.\n• Casper Juustovaara opened the scoring for Sweden.\n• Ivar Stenberg scored for Sweden.\n• Love Harenstam made 28 saves for Sweden.\n• Chase Reid, Will Zellers, and Teddy Stiga scored for the United States.\n• Brady Knowling stopped 23 shots for the United States before being replaced by Nick Kempf.\n• Sweden completed group play unbeaten.\n• The United States lost for the first time in the tournament.\n• In the quarterfinals on Friday, Sweden will play Latvia.\n• The United States will play Finland in the quarterfinals.\n• Canada will play Slovakia in the quarterfinals.\n• Czechia will meet Switzerland in the quarterfinals.\n• Canada defeated Finland 7-4.\n• Cole Beaudoin had two goals and an assist for Canada.\n• Brady Martin scored twice for Canada.\n• Zayne Parekh had a goal and two assists for Canada.\n• Switzerland beat Slovakia 3-2.\n• Czechia topped Latvia 4-2.",
